  "javadoc_description": "Class for fitting circular cross-sections around existing nodes of a Path in order to compute radii (node thickness) and midpoint refinement of existing coordinates. Thread Safety: When fitting multiple paths in parallel: 1. Call call() in parallel (thread-safe) 2. Call applyFit() sequentially (modifies path hierarchy)\n\nExample: \n```\nList<PathFitter> fitters = paths.stream()\n     .map(p -> new PathFitter(img, p))\n     .collect(Collectors.toList());\n <p>\n // Parallel fitting\n fitters.parallelStream().forEach(PathFitter::call);\n <p>\n // Sequential application\n fitters.forEach(PathFitter::applyFit);\n```\n",
